# What ./bootstrap.sh installs and checks out. Pins are the versions sae was
# last built and tested against, not "latest"; bump one in the same commit
# that needs it (or that re-verified sae against it), as the other Aether
# repos do with their own pins.

# Aether release. 0.778.0 is the first with what sae needs: the page engine,
# contrib.quickjs (aether#2418), with its amalgamation in the release tarball
# and in a source install (#2421), and quickjs.rethrow (#2420), which keeps
# the class of an exception a page's container block throws. The page veto
# needs the nested hide fix (#2381), in every release since 0.766.0.
# Verified: every suite green on a get.sh install of 0.778.0
# (SAE_AETHER_HOME=none ./build.sh).
# 0.791.0 (aether#2489 + #2511): sae's main() is Aether's, with no C entry
# file at all. aeb's c.program compiles it with --emit=lib, which keeps a
# program's main() as aether_main only from 0.789.0 (#2489), and the weak C
# main() that runs it in the linked program arrived with #2511 (released in
# 0.791.0); the same release carries the pure-Aether TLS client that
# std.http.client uses where there is no OpenSSL (sae on Android), the
# Android trust-store directories, and the rerun actor-leak fix.
# 0.801.0 (2026-10-10): a real floor move. contrib.sqlite's authorizer,
# limit, extension and column API (asks/sqlite-authorizer.md) replace the
# thirteen sqlite3_* externs and SQLite constants services/sqlite declared for
# itself, and contrib.quickjs's arg_bytes (asks/quickjs-typed-array-bytes.md)
# replaces src/sae_raster.c's AeQjs mirror, which is deleted; both arrived in
# 0.801.0. It also carries #2703 (a closure stored into a ptr field keeps its
# environment), which aether-ui's vg click handlers need from 0.796 on, and
# #2709's structured grants (.build.ae's `extern` cap). Verified against the
# dev tree at 0.801.0 (./build.sh). A bare get.sh install of 0.801.0
# (SAE_AETHER_HOME=none) does not link yet: the release ships contrib/sqlite's
# source but not its libaether_sqlite archive, which aether is fixing.
# 0.814.0 (2026-10-14): a real floor move. services/files and
# services/documents run each file operation inside std.sandbox's enforce,
# and until aether#2905 (released in 0.814.0) enforce left its checker
# installed after the block: from then on a path that could not be resolved
# was refused everywhere, the kernel's included. Verified: the dev tree at
# 0.814.0, run_all and the file specs (spec_app_caps, spec_app_documents,
# spec_app_sheet_files) on macOS and aether-linux.
# 0.818.0 (2026-10-16): a real floor move. 0.818's ownership rework
# (aether #2916/#2926) borrows a `ptr` parameter for the call unless it is
# declared `p: @keep ptr` (E0902); src/sae_host.ae and aevg now declare it
# on every one they keep (a page-API function's ctx, captured by the
# callbacks it registers, and the scene plumbing), and so does aether-ui.
# 0.817 and older cannot parse `@keep`. The bare release still does not
# link (no libaether_sqlite), so sae builds against a 0.818 dev tree.
# Verified: the dev tree at 0.818.0 (2a39e091), tests/run_all.sh 58/58 on
# macOS.
AE_PIN=0.818.0

